# Introductory group theory: cyclic and permutation groups, cosets and Lagrange, isomorphisms and products.
title "Group theory"
page a4 portrait margin=1cm
font 6pt..30pt
root core

node core "Groups"
| set G + operation
| associative, identity e, inverses
| order |G|, order |g|
| ℤ/nℤ, (ℤ/nℤ)ˣ, D₂ₙ of order 2n

node cyc "Cyclic\ngroups"
node perm "Permutation\ngroups"
node cos "Cosets and\nLagrange"
node iso "Isomorphisms\nand products"
node proofs "Proof\ntechniques"

node gen "Cyclic subgroup ⟨a⟩"
| ⟨a⟩ = {aᵏ : k ∈ ℤ}, negative k too.
| Smallest subgroup containing a.
| G cyclic ⟺ G = ⟨a⟩; a a generator.
| |a| = |⟨a⟩|.

node elord "Order of an element"
| aᵏ = e ⟺ |a| divides k.
| |aᵏ| = n / gcd(k, n).
| In ℤ/nℤ: ⟨k⟩ = ⟨gcd(k, n)⟩.

node divalg "Division Algorithm"
| a = bq + r, 0 ≤ r < b.
| With Well-Ordering, proves
| subgroups of cyclic are cyclic.

node abel "Cyclic ⇒ abelian"
| Converse false: (ℤ/8ℤ)ˣ.
| ℚ not cyclic.
| Subgroups of ℤ: nℤ, n ≥ 0.

node gens "Generators"
| aᵏ generates ⟺ gcd(k, n) = 1.
| φ(n) generators; in ℤ/nℤ: [k].
| Cyclic (ℤ/mℤ)ˣ: φ(φ(m)) generators.
| φ(pᵉ) = pᵉ − pᵉ⁻¹, multiplicative.

node ftcg "Subgroups of cyclic groups"
| Every subgroup cyclic.
| Exactly one subgroup per d | n: ⟨a^{n/d}⟩.

node polar "Complex numbers"
| a + bi = re^{iθ}, r = √(a² + b²).
| Moduli multiply, angles add.
| DeMoivre: (re^{iθ})ⁿ = rⁿe^{inθ}.

node roots "Roots"
| zⁿ = Re^{iθ}: R^{1/n}e^{i(θ+2πk)/n}.
| nth roots of unity = ⟨e^{2πi/n}⟩.
| Primitive: e^{2πik/n}, gcd(k, n) = 1.

node sn "Symmetric group Sₙ"
| Bijections of {1..n}; |Sₙ| = n!.
| στ: τ first, then σ (right to left).
| k-cycle (a₁ … aₖ); transposition = 2-cycle.
| Disjoint cycle form; disjoint commute.

node ord "Orders in Sₙ"
| |σ| = lcm of cycle lengths.
| Cycle types = partitions of n.
| S₄: 1, 2, 3, 4. S₅, S₆: up to 6.
| (a₁ … aₖ)⁻¹ = (aₖ … a₁).

node count "Counting in Sₙ"
| #k-cycles = n! / ((n − k)! · k).
| #cyclic subgroups of order p
| = #(order-p elements) / (p − 1).
| S₄ has a subgroup of every d | 24.

node parity "Parity"
| k-cycle = k − 1 transpositions.
| Even/odd well-defined.
| k-cycle even ⟺ k odd.

node an "Alternating group Aₙ"
| Even permutations; |Aₙ| = n!/2.
| Generated by 3-cycles.
| A₄: orders 1, 2, 3 only.

node dih "Dihedral group D₂ₙ"
| {rᵏ, rᵏs}: rⁿ = s² = e, srs = r⁻¹.
| srᵏ = r⁻ᵏs; every rᵏs has order 2.
| Center: {e} (n odd), {e, r^{n/2}} (n even).
| Cube motions ≅ S₄.

node cosets "Cosets"
| gH = {gh}, Hg = {hg}; in ℤ/nℤ: a + H.
| Cosets partition G; |gH| = |H|.
| [G : H] = #left = #right cosets.

node crit "Coset criteria"
| g₁H = g₂H ⟺ Hg₁⁻¹ = Hg₂⁻¹
| ⟺ g₁H ⊆ g₂H ⟺ g₂ ∈ g₁H
| ⟺ g₁⁻¹g₂ ∈ H. So gH = H ⟺ g ∈ H.

node ex "Cosets in examples"
| List: take uncovered g, form gH, repeat.
| In Sₙ, gH: h acts first, then g.
| S₄ by ⟨(1234)⟩, V, ⟨(123)⟩.
| S₃ ≤ S₄: left ≠ right cosets.

node normal "Normal subgroups"
| H ⊴ G: ghg⁻¹ ∈ H for all g, h.
| ⇒ gH = Hg for all g.
| Abelian or index 2 ⇒ normal.
| gH = Hg does not force gh = hg.

node lagr "Lagrange's Theorem"
| H ≤ G finite ⇒ |H| divides |G|.
| |G| = [G : H]·|H|.
| [G : K] = [G : H][H : K].

node corr "Corollaries"
| |g| divides |G|; g^{|G|} = e.
| |G| = p ⇒ cyclic, any g ≠ e generates.
| gcd(|H|, |K|) = 1 ⇒ H ∩ K = {e}.

node euler "Euler and Fermat"
| gcd(a, n) = 1 ⇒ a^{φ(n)} ≡ 1 (mod n).
| p ∤ a ⇒ a^{p−1} ≡ 1 (mod p); bᵖ ≡ b.
| Reduce exponent mod φ(n), not n.
| Repeated squaring for aᵏ mod n.

node conv "Converse fails"
| d | |G| does not force
| a subgroup of order d:
| A₄ has none of order 6.

node isodef "Isomorphism"
| Bijection, φ(ab) = φ(a)φ(b).
| φ(e) = e, φ(a⁻¹) = φ(a)⁻¹, |φ(a)| = |a|.
| ≅ is an equivalence relation.

node invar "Invariants (prove ≇)"
| Order, abelian, cyclic,
| # elements of each order, center.
| D₈ ≇ Q₈, S₃ ≇ ℤ/6ℤ,
| ℤ/4ℤ ≇ ℤ/2ℤ × ℤ/2ℤ.

node classif "Classification"
| Infinite cyclic ≅ ℤ; order n ≅ ℤ/nℤ.
| |G| = p ⇒ G ≅ ℤ/pℤ.
| Order 6: ℤ/6ℤ or S₃.

node cayley "Cayley's Theorem"
| Every group ≅ a group of
| permutations, via g ↦ (x ↦ gx).

node prod "Direct products"
| |(g, h)| = lcm(|g|, |h|).
| ℤ/mℤ × ℤ/nℤ ≅ ℤ/mnℤ ⟺ gcd(m, n) = 1.
| Internal: G = HK, H ∩ K = {e},
| hk = kh ⇒ G ≅ H × K.

node units "Unit groups"
| (ℤ/nℤ)ˣ: units mod n, order φ(n).
| Identify: list unit orders, match
| against products of ℤ/dℤ.
| (ℤ/8ℤ)ˣ ≅ (ℤ/12ℤ)ˣ; (ℤ/24ℤ)ˣ ≅ (ℤ/2ℤ)³.

node subtest "Subgroup tests"
| H ≠ ∅ and ab⁻¹ ∈ H ⇒ H ≤ G.
| Finite H: closure is enough.
| Intersections of subgroups
| are subgroups.

node counting "Counting arguments"
| Cosets partition G: sum their sizes.
| Order-p elements come in
| groups of p − 1.
| |G| even ⇒ some g ≠ e has g = g⁻¹.

node structure "Proving structure"
| Exhibit a generator ⇒ cyclic.
| Every g² = e ⇒ abelian.
| No proper nontrivial subgroups
| ⇒ cyclic of prime order.

node disprove "Prove or disprove"
| Counterexamples: (ℤ/8ℤ)ˣ,
| ℤ/2ℤ × ℤ/2ℤ, S₃, ℚ, A₄.
| Salvage: add the missing hypothesis.

core -> cyc perm cos iso proofs
cyc -> gen polar
gen -> elord divalg abel
elord -> gens ftcg
polar -> roots
perm -> sn dih
sn -> ord parity
ord -> count
parity -> an
cos -> cosets lagr normal
cosets -> crit ex
lagr -> corr euler conv
iso -> isodef prod
isodef -> invar classif cayley
prod -> units
proofs -> subtest counting structure disprove

divalg ..> ftcg "proof"
corr ..> classif "|G| = p"
conv ..> an "counterexample"
